Keep device example selection independent of pytest's automatic IDs

pytest 9.2 replaces string parameters longer than 100 characters with IDs such
as sample0. Device example parameters contain absolute paths longer than that,
so the harness's `-k "numba_cuda_mlir and not perf"` filter selects no examples.

Use explicit paths relative to examples/device as IDs. They preserve the backend
and filename for selection without depending on the checkout location or pytest's
long-string ID strategy. Keep the harness's zero-tests guard unchanged.

Drop this patch once nvmath-python supplies explicit backend-qualified example IDs.
Applied by ci/tools/run-nvmath-python-mlir-tests.

diff --git a/tests/example_tests/device_tests/test_device_samples.py b/tests/example_tests/device_tests/test_device_samples.py
--- a/tests/example_tests/device_tests/test_device_samples.py
+++ b/tests/example_tests/device_tests/test_device_samples.py
@@ -39,7 +39,11 @@ fp16_examples = {
 }
 
 
-@pytest.mark.parametrize("sample", sample_files)
+@pytest.mark.parametrize(
+    "sample",
+    sample_files,
+    ids=[os.path.relpath(sample, samples_path) for sample in sample_files],
+)
 class TestDeviceSamples:
     def test_sample(self, sample, request):
         ctk_version = get_nvrtc_version()
